{
  "_comment": {
    "about": "2.971.0 360 PANORAMA (the image editor's Image > 360 Panorama): Qwen Image 2.1 + the community 360 panorama outpaint LoRA (nomadoor/qwen-image-2.1-360-panorama-outpaint-lora, qwen_image_2_1_360_panorama_outpaint_lora_v0_1.safetensors, strength 0.8 - node 11, LoraLoaderModelOnly as in nomadoor's example, a LoRA slot the job's style fills; Qwen Research License: non-commercial). LoadImage 21 = the 2:1 equirectangular canvas bitGen builds (ext/imageeditdock/pcpano.js): the pictures where they were placed, PURE GREEN #00FF00 everywhere else; the model fills the green. Its card: 2048 x 1024, 25 steps, cfg 1, the prompt begins with the trigger sentence. The same graph as ComfyUI-Panorama-Stickers' example (nomadoor, MIT) with Panorama Studio replaced by bitGen's own canvas, so no custom node pack is needed.",
    "credits": "https://github.com/nomadoor/ComfyUI-Panorama-Stickers (MIT) - example_workflows/qwen-image-2.1-360-erp-outpaint.json, commit 732146a"
  },
  "1": {
    "class_type": "UNETLoader",
    "inputs": {
      "unet_name": "qwen_image_2.1_int8_convrot.safetensors",
      "weight_dtype": "default"
    },
    "_meta": {
      "title": "Qwen Image 2.1"
    }
  },
  "2": {
    "class_type": "CLIPLoader",
    "inputs": {
      "clip_name": "qwen3vl_8b_int8_convrot.safetensors",
